WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.850
- So many women are dealing
with life after divorce.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.032
I know because I am one of them

00:00:07.032 --> 00:00:10.990
Adjusting to a new life, it is not easy.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:15.001
It takes almost years to
figure out how to navigate it.

00:00:15.001 --> 00:00:17.016
And it's a taboo subject.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.610
And here on this show,

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.028
we wanna be gentle and we
wanna figure things out

00:00:23.028 --> 00:00:26.090
and we wanna support each other

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:30.470
and learn from each other's
life experiences and wisdom.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:31.830
And with that,

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.000
I wanna introduce Louanna,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.787
who is currently dealing with divorce.

00:00:36.787 --> 00:00:39.190
Please take a look.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.600
- Hi Drew, this is Louanna.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.990
I'm going through a really
tough divorce situation

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:45.823
right now,

00:00:45.823 --> 00:00:47.610
and I know you've been
through the same thing.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:51.620
I've been married for 11 years,
separated for three years,

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.910
I have three beautiful children,

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:57.200
but I think everything's
just in limbo right now.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.990
I mean the pandemic has put a hold

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:02.790
on every single thing
that needs to be done.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.200
I'm just,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.730
I'm a single mom and I'm
just trying to stay positive.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.270
I'm taking it one day at a time,

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.320
counting my blessings each and every day.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.080
But I know that you can help me.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.405
So could we please talk about this?

00:01:17.405 --> 00:01:19.550
(audience clapping)

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.590
Louanna I would be
honored to talk about it.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.135
Hi, how are you?

00:01:24.135 --> 00:01:24.968
(audience clapping)

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:25.801
- Hello, hello.

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:26.634
Good morning.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:27.891
Thank you for having me.

00:01:27.891 --> 00:01:30.100
- I'm gonna just start
right out of the gate

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.560
and say that your smiling
eyes and your tone,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.160
tone is a big thing with me,

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.400
and it's synonymous with energy.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.233
- [Louanna] Right.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.710
- And your energy is clearly
seeking the light here

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:46.760
and wherever it took you
to get to where you are,

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.284
you are in a place
where you are projecting

00:01:49.284 --> 00:01:52.680
and radiating strength and light.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.400
So I commend you for the
immense amount of work

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.603
it must've taken you to get
where you are right now.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:04.340
- It has been a journey, but
I'm happy that I'm here now.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.550
I always told myself that
there is a light at the end

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:08.383
of the tunnel,

00:02:08.383 --> 00:02:10.820
and I just have to feel to heal.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:15.430
So I was open to feeling
any pain, any happiness,

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:18.940
any ups and downs, any joy,
whatever I felt that day,

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.120
I made sure to feel it
at a hundred percent

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.720
just so I know that I
went through the journey

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.274
to get me to where I am right now.

00:02:24.274 --> 00:02:27.199
- How long were you married may I ask?

00:02:27.199 --> 00:02:31.670
- I was married for 11 years
and kind of still right?

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:35.590
'Cause you know, the
divorce is still pending.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.550
I'm in limbo.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.116
And so I am still married,

00:02:39.116 --> 00:02:43.260
but I was together with
my ex for about 11 years.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.293
- And how long has it been
since you've been separated?

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.440
- About three, about three,
maybe going into four

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.380
'cause my youngest
daughter is four years old.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.380
So yeah, since then.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.873
- And where, divorce papers aside,

00:02:58.873 --> 00:03:02.650
where do you feel like
you're at in the journey?

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:05.640
Do you still feel like
everything is as raw and fresh

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:06.859
as if it was yesterday,

00:03:06.859 --> 00:03:09.900
or do you feel like the
ship is leaving the dock

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.023
a little bit?

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.300
The ship has almost left the dock.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.380
I can't say that I'm a
hundred percent there,

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:22.151
but I certainly do not
feel the same way as I did

00:03:22.151 --> 00:03:23.916
a few years back.

00:03:23.916 --> 00:03:28.267
So time does heal and I'm
happy that I'm here now.

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:31.500
- I'm so glad to hear you
say that because everybody

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.080
said that to me, time.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.840
I think the way you described
it was really good and it, it,

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.405
I think what nobody talks
about is that it's gonna take

00:03:40.405 --> 00:03:43.710
probably a lot more time
than you really want it to

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:44.545
or anticipate.

00:03:44.545 --> 00:03:47.280
- Yes it does take a little bit longer,

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.540
because we are as mothers,

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.386
we have that connection
with their fathers,

00:03:51.386 --> 00:03:54.710
so we can't really say it's
out of sight out of mind.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:55.680
We still have that connection.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.076
We still have to interact with them.

00:03:57.076 --> 00:03:58.987
So it does take a little bit longer,

00:03:58.987 --> 00:04:02.060
and but as long as it,

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:04.110
you'll get to where you need to go,

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.640
then it should be fine.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:11.640
- I think it takes such
a intricately woven art

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.760
to navigate divorce with
children and how we talk

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:20.175
to those children and
how we work with our exes

00:04:20.175 --> 00:04:23.051
in front of them or to them.

00:04:23.051 --> 00:04:25.593
How are you doing with that part?

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:29.940
- It was difficult in the
beginning because my emotions

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:31.533
and my feelings were so strong,

00:04:31.533 --> 00:04:33.633
but I had to keep thinking to myself,

00:04:33.633 --> 00:04:37.400
especially from advice
from family and friends

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.860
that keep your children
the number one priority.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.000
What is best for them,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.149
and that's what you should do.

00:04:44.149 --> 00:04:47.947
Not to say that you have to
forget about your feelings,

00:04:47.947 --> 00:04:50.768
but just keep them number one.

00:04:50.768 --> 00:04:54.052
Make sure what they see is positivity

00:04:54.052 --> 00:04:57.709
and that no matter what
the differences are,

00:04:57.709 --> 00:04:59.970
and we do have differences,

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:02.300
you know co-parenting difficulties

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:06.261
that we have disagreements
about a lot of things.

00:05:06.261 --> 00:05:08.555
For example, education.

00:05:08.555 --> 00:05:12.230
I'm the big believer in sending
my kids to Catholic school,

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:13.330
where he isn't.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.020
So there's one disagreement,

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:17.560
but we have to act as
adults and he and I have

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:21.380
to be very mature and just
kind of do that on the side,

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.790
and it's almost like putting up a show.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.170
And my kids are probably
too young to even understand

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:27.003
what I'm saying right now,

00:05:27.003 --> 00:05:30.530
but you're kind of
putting, putting a front,

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.690
you know in front of
them just to make sure

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:36.061
that they're seeing the
positive vibes going on.

00:05:36.061 --> 00:05:38.440
- I know that this is so hard,

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.720
but I think you're at an amazing place,

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:45.520
a really inspirational place
that I'm sure took years

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:47.353
and really hard work to get to.

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:51.070
- Yes, that I could definitely agree too.

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:55.390
And I take a lot of my strength
from the women who I know

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:57.310
are with me on this,

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:59.600
'cause I know there are
women out there who feel

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:00.881
the same way as I do.

00:06:00.881 --> 00:06:05.520
And I know that I have a team
backing me up just like you.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:08.200
I know you're behind me and
I'm behind you all the way,

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.560
and we support each other.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:12.250
So I take a lot of my
strength from the other women

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:14.010
around me and the other women who I know

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:15.368
are going through the same thing,

00:06:15.368 --> 00:06:18.035
(upbeat music)

